00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Well, I'm sure you've heard in the national news

95
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
this past week that the BSA

96
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
is considering a change in its membership policy.

97
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,000
This change basically has two parts.

98
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
The first would be our national organization

99
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
would no longer consider sexual orientation

100
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
as a barrier to membership.

101
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
The second part of it is that this change

102
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,000
would allow religious, civic or educational organizations

103
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,000
that oversee and deliver Scouting

104
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
to determine how to address the issue,

105
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,000
and that the BSA would not under any circumstances

106
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,000
dictate a position to their units, members or parents,

107
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,000
And they would not require any chartered organization

108
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:08,000
to act in ways inconsistent with that organization's

109
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
mission or principles or religious beliefs.

110
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
I've written about my take on that

111
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,000
at ScoutmasterCGcom

112
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:18,000
and there's been a lively discussion that followed.

113
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Not everybody's happy.

114
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
If you're a regular reader or listener,

115
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:25,000
you know that I have declined to make membership policies

116
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:30,000
a part of the open discussion at ScoutmasterCGcom,

117
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,000
And so this represents a little policy change of my own,

118
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Perhaps not national news,

119
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,000
but I think it's going to be important,

120
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
if this policy changes, for us to be able to discuss it,

121
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,000
And I think it's going to be important to do it

122
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,000
in a moderate way.

123
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
I mean, naturally this has the potential

124
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
to be a divisive issue,

125
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:50,000
but I think our job as Scouters is to find a way forward

126
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,000
where we can all continue to serve our Scouts,

127
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,000
be loyal to our national organization

128
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
and be loyal to the principles

129
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
of the worldwide movement of Scouting.

130
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,000
I'm sure there's going to be much more for us

131
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,000
as time goes by,

132
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,000
But podcast 157 is going out

133
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,000
before the absolute change to this policy has been announced,

134
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
So I think we'll leave it there for now.

