206
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Scout Mastership in 7 Minutes

207
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
or Less?

208
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
So every once in a while

209
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,000
I'll hear somebody talk about competition

210
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,000
in scouting,

211
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
And competition is not a bad thing in itself-

212
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,000
not at all-

213
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,000
But I'm going to suggest that the idea

214
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,000
of there always being a clear winner

215
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
and a clear loser

216
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
is probably not what we want to use

217
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
when we talk about competition in scouting.

218
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Boys are naturally competitive.

219
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,000
They like to win

220
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,000
and they hate to lose.

221
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
Competing is not bad in itself,

222
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,000
but misapplied,

223
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
I think the competition

224
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
can be kind of corrosive,

225
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,000
especially with younger boys.

226
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Winning is not always all it's cracked up to be

227
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:23,000
and losing is definitely not always bad.

228
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,000
We learn from doing things

229
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,000
and giving them a try

230
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,000
and making mistakes sometimes.

231
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Scouting is designed to recognize

232
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,000
not only achievement

233
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,000
but effort.

234
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Competition is a tool.

235
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,000
it's a means to an end,

236
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,000
but it's not an end in itself.

237
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,000
The level of achievement

238
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,000
in scouting

239
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,000
is nowhere near as important

240
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,000
as the effort that gets extended towards that.

241
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:48,000
What one person can achieve easily

242
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:51,000
may take somebody else a lot of effort to match.

243
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
What we want to do

244
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,000
is encourage effort and confidence

245
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,000
in individuals and in the group.

246
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,000
Baden Powell said this.

247
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,000
boys are especially sensitive

248
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,000
to measures of achievement and failures.

249
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,000
It is the scout master's job

250
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,000
to put these things

251
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
into perspective for his boys.

252
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,000
The boy whose inferiority complex

253
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:13,000
has been born through many failures,

254
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,000
can have his first win or two

255
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,000
made easy for him

256
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:20,000
so that he is led to intensify his efforts.

257
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
If he extends the effort,

258
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,000
no matter how clumsy,

259
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,000
he can earn the badge.

260
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:28,000
This generally inspires the boy to go on trying

261
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,000
and the sense of inferiority

262
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
fades quickly.

263
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
You know, we're not all equally talented and gifted.

264
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,000
We can all extend effort

265
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,000
to attain a goal.

266
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,000
When we're young,

267
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
we need to learn to deal with dissatisfaction

268
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,000
and disappointment

269
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
by assessing the effort we extended,

270
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
recognizing how we can improve

271
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,000
and then redoubling the effort.

272
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Scouts need to compete right

273
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
And they will compete,

274
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
And trying to stop them from competing

275
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,000
is absolutely fruitless.

276
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,000
But what we do, as Baden Powell said,

277
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,000
is put all this into perspective

278
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:02,000
and show our scouts that it's not really

279
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,000
whether you win or lose,

280
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,000
but how you play the game.

281
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:08,000
It's not really about just achieving,

282
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,000
but it's about developing resilience

283
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,000
and the ability to encourage yourself,

284
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,000
to look for that effort,

285
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:17,000
to know that, okay, I'm not as talented

286
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
and skilled in every single thing

287
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
as everybody else,

288
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,000
but I can put some effort into

289
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,000
becoming a better person.

290
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:27,000
If we create an environment

291
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
that celebrates achievement

292
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,000
and effort equally,

293
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,000
I think we've really done something

294
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
and will really be helping our scouts,

295
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Boy Scouts,

296
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,000
Boy Scouts,

297
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Boy Scouts.

298
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Find me a letter,

299
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
send it by name

300
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Email. that is, folks.

301
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:09,000
And here's an answer to one of your emails.

302
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Email came in asking me

303
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,000
what I thought about offering

304
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
eagle-required maripages

305
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:21,000
on maripage days.

306
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Now you know what I'm talking about here.

307
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,000
These are these big events

308
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,000
where they may have like a,

309
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
they may offer a number of maripages

310
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
on a Saturday or something like that.

311
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:33,000
The person who sent me this email

312
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
says that they have a troop rule

313
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,000
that none of their scouts

314
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,000
are allowed to participate in.

315
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
The person writing said:

316
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
we've had this rule for a long time.

317
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
We have a good base of counselors

318
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
within the troop that offer

319
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
eagle-required maripages,

320
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
And I don't want scouts

321
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,000
seeing an easy way out,

322
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,000
And I've seen some things happen

323
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
at these maripage days

324
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
that I don't consider to be

325
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,000
proper maripage counseling.

326
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,000
So I'm going to agree

327
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,000
with the person who challenged

328
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
this rule in your troop

329
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
and I'm going to tell you

330
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,000
that you're outside of policy on this one.

331
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,000
A scout gets to choose

332
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
his maripage counselor.

333
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
So long as a counselor is registered,

334
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,000
there's no reason to prevent him

335
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
from using that counselor

336
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:23,000
And there's certainly no policy

337
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,000
to back up the idea that you can.

338
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,000
A recent change to the maripage application,

339
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,000
the blue card- made it clear

340
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,000
that scoutmasters and

341
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
unit leaders are not

342
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,000
pre-qualifying a scout

343
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,000
to take a maripage,

344
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,000
but that they're just making sure

345
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,000
that the scout is going to be working

346
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,000
with a registered counselor.

347
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,000
Now if you have concerns

348
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,000
over the way a particular maripage

349
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,000
is being counseled by a particular counselor,

350
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,000
well then you go

351
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,000
to your district or

352
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
council advancement committee

353
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,000
and you share your concerns with them,

354
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
because they're the ones who vet

355
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
and certify people to be maripage counselors.

356
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,000
There is one way

357
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:05,000
for a scout to earn a maripage

358
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,000
and that is to go to a counselor

359
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
to complete the requirements

360
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,000
to have the counselor certify it, and we're done.

361
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,000
It's really not our place

362
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,000
to question the quality of a scout's work

363
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,000
on a maripage, because that's the

364
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,000
maripage counselor's job.

365
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,000
And I'll repeat myself: if you think

366
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,000
a particular maripage counselor

367
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,000
is not doing a very good job of it,

368
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,000
well go to whoever

369
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,000
certified them and bring that up.

370
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,000
Scouts should be free to choose

371
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
the place or the time or the counselor.

372
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Eagle-required maripages

373
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,000
are no different from any other maripage,

374
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:39,000
other than the fact that they're required

375
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,000
to become an eagle scout. I don't think

376
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,000
they need to be offered with any greater

377
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
or lesser rigor than any other maripage.

378
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
and I'll add this

379
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,000
while I have the chance:

380
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,000
There are no greater or lesser eagle

381
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,000
scouts. The way a scout becomes an eagle

382
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,000
is they do the

383
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,000
requirements and they pass

384
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,000
a duly constituted border review.

385
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
There's no advanced eagle scouts

386
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
and there's no lesser eagle scouts,

387
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
There's only eagle scouts.

388
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
in the same way, There's no scout

389
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
that gets an advanced maripage,

390
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
There's only maripages.

391
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
And once again, if the question

392
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
of the suitability of a counselor comes up,

393
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,000
go to the people who vet the counselor.

394
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,000
I think that a rule like this

395
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
is kind of inimical to the idea of

396
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,000
the maripage system.

397
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,000
It's definitely outside of policy

398
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,000
and I would just continue

399
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,000
doing it. That's my advice to you,

400
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,000
and if you have a question,

401
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
you can get in touch and you'll find out

402
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
